"Caldwell is white-bright-power to the augera, and calls himself loyal opposition to the Fateweavers."
"Caldwell is bound by the Major Prophecy in a minor role and cannot go against it."
"Caldwell phases through oblivion so he seems to teleport, and reads the threads of Fate."
"With Reeves and the Spires, Caldwell wove the Empire-wide wipe of the Chosen One's identity."
"Caldwell urged the Emperor to call up arcanists, and fears the Prophecy's 'mortal thrones'."
"Caldwell tutors Caden in secret for a future favour, and hides the gap in the web around him."
"Caldwell bound the Academy augera to silence toward Caden until Caden speaks to it first."
"Caldwell wants the Empire properly preserved or properly destroyed."
"Now: Caldwell is otherwise engaged this week, most likely in the Spire; sessions resume at weekend."
"Caldwell's wysana is a nameless, curt construct of pure arcana that refuses any name."
"The wysana's core is bound to Caldwell's staff; it dwells in oblivion and dips into the world."
"The wysana runs the library cafe and campus services and knows each patron's wants."
"The wysana conjures meals and clothes, moves things unseen, and spars with Caden in training."
"Now: the wysana serves the library cafe and carries Caldwell's messages to Caden in the Vault."
"Reeves has ties to the Fateweavers, and kept his memories when they wiped Caden from his friends."
